Parts of the DSP in this folder follow Mutable Instruments designs released under the MIT licence:
- the wow and flutter model in src/tape_echo_core.cc (TapeEcho::Control) is Beads' WowAndFlutter
  (https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack, beads/dsp), rewritten in integers in coldsoldr/te-op1-cfw
  (ports/fx/src/tape_echo);
- the half-rate output stage in src/half_rate.h, src/halfband.cc and src/halfband_bfin.S (the crossfade tables
  and the soft limit) is Clouds' (clouds/dsp, with stmlib), in coldsoldr/te-op1-cfw's fixed-point port
  (ports/clouds/src/core).
Those parts are released under the same terms as the originals. The rest (tape_echo.cc, the tape echo itself, the
kernels) is coldsoldr's, GPL-3.0-or-later with the OP-1 firmware permission (see ../../LICENSE and ../../NOTICE); the
plugin file built from them is conveyed under the GPL, which the MIT terms allow.

